@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Testing strategy — four layers, speed traded for fidelity

component "**1. Unit**\ninternal/*/*_test.go — no build tags\nGo only · deterministic\n//always//" as L1 <<app>>
component "**2. Contract**\nGo builders + goldens\nDockerRunArgs · BuildPlan · Detect · writeBrokerEnv\n//always, no Docker//" as L2 <<app>>
component "**3. Infra integration**\ninternal/egress ""//go:build integration//""\nreal containers, no model\n//-tags=integration + PROVEO_EGRESS_INTEGRATION=1//" as L3 <<async>>
component "**4. Agent E2E (promptful)**\ntests/e2e ""//go:build e2e//"" via internal/tmux\nnon-deterministic — asserts side effects\n//-tags=e2e · skips per missing prerequisite//" as L4 <<async>>

database "cov/unit\ngo tool covdata merge → percent" as COV <<db>>

L1 ARROW_MAIN L2
L2 ARROW_MAIN L3
L3 ARROW_MAIN L4
L1 ARROW_QUEUE COV
L2 ARROW_QUEUE COV

note right of L1
  Host orchestration under test is **Go**
  (""cmd/proveo"", ""internal/{runner,workspace,egress,
  dind,gitidentity,manifest}""). Fat bash runners and the
  ""defs/lib/egress.sh"" lifecycle are retired.
end note

note right of L2
  **Go-first contracts:** execute the builders and diff
  the argv/plan, rather than grepping source for literal
  strings. A grep contract survives the deletion of the
  thing it claimed to test — it passes while testing
  nothing. Bash remains only for image smoke suites.
end note

note right of L4
  **Know which rendering an assertion reads.**
  Two backends render one launch, so a docker-only
  expectation applied to both stays red on the
  sandbox; and a restated image tag stops matching
  the container the day the tag policy moves.
end note

note right of L3
  Topology is owned (""BuildPlan"" + ""ExecRunner""), so do
  **not** add testcontainers-go for Squid/proxy. Apply
  its //practices// instead: wait on the CA file / HTTP
  ready (never sleep-only), ""t.Cleanup"" teardown, env
  gate + ""docker"" LookPath skip.
end note

note right of L4
  Two suites, different credentials:
  * ""e2e_test.go"" — local model (Ollama), opencode,
    broker mode; keyless and CI-honest
  * ""hello_world_test.go"" — cloud model, all three
    targets, firewall + credential broker
  Both assert **side effects on the host**, never the
  model's prose. See 42-hello-world-e2e.puml.
end note

note bottom of COV
  Default ""go test ./..."" never compiles Layer 3/4 — the
  PR path stays fast and keyless. No hard coverage gate
  until a baseline exists; CI publishes the percent as an
  artifact.

  **Deferred (Stage 0b):** ""proveo/egress-proxy:cover""
  from ""go build -cover"" + a bind-mounted ""GOCOVERDIR"",
  so Layer 3 reports statement coverage from inside the
  container. Topology coverage does not require it.
end note

' --- IGNORE: layout hints (do not edit) ---
L1 -down[hidden]- L2
L3 -down[hidden]- L4
' --- END IGNORE ---
note as ECHOAGENT
  **The Layer-4 promptful E2E runs against a fixture agent, not a vendor
  CLI.** ""defs/tests/echo-agent"" is a minimal image that reads a prompt and
  calls the local model through the OpenAI-compatible endpoint
  ""--local-model"" already provides — so the suite exercises proveo's own
  wiring (mounts, egress, model routing) without a paid API key or a
  vendor's release cadence in the loop.
end note


note as DEFTESTS
  **Each def ships its own container test suite**, and they share a shape:
  a helper that runs a command inside the built image and captures output
  for assertions, plus a portable timeout — GNU ships ""timeout"", macOS
  ships it as ""gtimeout"" via coreutils, and where neither exists the suite
  degrades rather than failing on the tooling.

  Two habits worth keeping when editing them. The entrypoint is exercised
  by mounting a fixture project and **short-circuiting the final exec**
  (an unsupported flag that exits immediately), so a TUI launch does not
  hang a test. And several assertions have to tolerate the harness CLI
  normalising its own config on launch — cursor rewrites
  ""~/\.cursor/cli-config\.json"" every start and backs up an invalid one as
  ""\.bad"", so a test asserting on a config file must account for the CLI
  having touched it.
end note


@enduml
